WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.530
When The Empire Strikes Back first hit cinemas
in 1980, audiences didn't yet know that Luke

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.960
and Leia were twins, or that Darth Vader was
their father.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.340
So when Leia kissed Luke early in the movie
in an effort to make Han Solo jealous, it

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.730
was played as a joke that introduced some
mild romantic tension between the three main

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.280
characters, and upped the will-they-won't-they
stakes of Leia and Han's relationship.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:31.600
It was only three years later, in Return of
the Jedi, that Luke and Leia learned that

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.180
they were actually siblings, making that kiss
appear a little incestuous in hindsight.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.840
"Yoda spoke of another."

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.940
"The other he spoke of is your twin sister."

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:50.170
But if you still cringe thinking about that
kiss, just know that it could have been so

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.170
much worse.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:56.899
Thanks to a deleted scene that was released
on Disney+ in November 2019, we now know that

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.880
the relationship between Luke and Leia almost
got even more inappropriate.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:07.100
In the version of the scene we all know, Han
and Chewbacca come to the medical bay to say

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:12.219
goodbye to Luke, who's recovering from his
near-death experience with the wampa.

00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:17.810
Luke looks uncomfortable when Han insists
that Leia has feelings for him, and Leia comes

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.820
back with an iconic insult.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.940
"Why you stuck-up, half-witted, scruffy looking
nerf-herder."

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.360
Finally, Leia brusquely kisses Luke in front
of Han, then exits triumphantly.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.540
But in the deleted scene, it's made clear
that Luke wasn't just uncomfortable because

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:37.310
he felt like a third wheel.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.560
In that version, we learn that he was actually
jealous of Leia and Han's obvious romantic

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.280
tension, after his near-death experience awakened
Luke to his romantic feelings for Leia.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.800
"It got me thinking, you know.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.340
I might never get the chance to…"

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:03.100
Luke tries to explain how he feels, but when
he goes in for a kiss, the ever-reliable C-3PO

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.720
interrupts.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.960
The moment gone, Luke tells Leia that he plans
to leave.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.000
She accuses him of deserting her and the Resistance,
just like Han, who then arrives with Chewbacca,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.040
and the original scene plays out.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.790
Yes, the kiss is already bad once you know
that Luke and Leia are siblings.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.840
But this longer version introduces a love
triangle subplot that would have created a

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.379
totally different dynamic in the movies.

00:02:28.379 --> 00:02:33.909
Luke secretly being infatuated with Leia would
have thrown a major wedge between the three

00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:39.209
main characters and potentially stalled his
Jedi training, since Jedi frown on trivial

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:40.420
matters like love.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.260
Interestingly, series creator George Lucas
has remained quiet on whether or not he knew

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:48.680
that Luke and Leia were siblings during the
making of Empire.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.879
If he already had that plot twist figured
out, it would explain why he decided that

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.329
this would-be romance had to go.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:01.000
However, while Lucas has deftly avoided the
subject of this particular lost storyline,

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.749
he does like to hint that he knew how the
Star Wars saga would play out all along.

00:03:05.749 --> 00:03:10.450
That would mean that he's fine having siblings
smooch when they don't know they're related,

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.030
but not with one declaring a full-on crush
on the other.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.560
However, there is some evidence that Luke
and Leia weren't yet identified as siblings

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.330
by this point in the franchise.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:25.859
The fact that they got as far as filming the
deleted version of the medical bay scene suggests

00:03:25.859 --> 00:03:30.499
that there was some question about what kind
of relationship the two characters were going

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:31.000
to have.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.440
Plus, in earlier drafts of the Empire script,
Vader was going to play on Luke's romantic

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.849
feelings for Leia to turn him to the Dark
Side.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:44.060
Luke was still supposed to have a sister in
these earlier drafts, although she was meant

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.749
to be a totally new character who wasn't going
to appear until Return of the Jedi.

00:03:48.749 --> 00:03:54.300
But the theory goes that this extra character
proved to be just too much for a story already

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.709
teeming with subplots.

00:03:55.709 --> 00:04:00.549
Instead, after Leia confessed her love for
Han at the end of Empire, Lucas decided to

00:04:00.549 --> 00:04:06.560
kill two Stormtroopers with one blaster shot
and just have Leia be Luke's sister, making

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.769
Star Wars easier for everyone.

